   "source": [
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "Variance-homogeneity diagnostics on log10 RAAS across age groups (Bartlett + Levene)\n",
    "Equal variance across ages is the assumption behind the equal-variance Student t-test (3a-i) and Dunnett\n",
    "(3a-ii). Bartlett assumes normality; Levene (center='median') is robust to non-normality -> trust Levene\n",
    "over Bartlett when the QQ diagnostics above show heavy tails. Reported at two levels:\n",
    "  (A) PER-SAAP -- the assumption check that actually licenses the per-SAAP tests: both tests run within each\n",
    "                  tissue x SAAP across its age groups (n~4/age), summarized as the % of SAAPs rejecting H0.\n",
    "  (B) POOLED   -- one Bartlett/Levene per comparison on ALL replicate RAAS pooled per age (the literal\n",
    "                  template translation). NOTE: pooling mixes SAAP-to-SAAP spread into the \"variance\", so\n",
    "                  this answers \"does overall RAAS spread differ by age\", not the per-SAAP assumption.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "AGE_ORDER    = ['t06mo', 't15mo', 't24mo', 't30mo']\n",
    "BASELINE_AGE = 't06mo'                                    # young reference (\"normal\")\n",
    "AGED_AGES    = [a for a in AGE_ORDER if a != BASELINE_AGE]\n",
    "MIN_REPS     = 3                                          # min mice/group to test a SAAP in a tissue (of 4)\n",
    "SIG_ALPHA    = 0.05\n",
    "\n",
    "# (A) per-SAAP: distribution of variance-test p-values across tissue x SAAP groups (all available ages)\n",
    "bartlett_p_saap, levene_p_saap = [], []\n",
    "for tissue, keys, by_age, _ in iter_saaps():\n",
    "    ages = [a for a in AGE_ORDER if len(by_age.get(a, [])) >= MIN_REPS]\n",
    "    if len(ages) < 2:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    arrs = [by_age[a] for a in ages]\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        bartlett_p_saap.append(stats.bartlett(*arrs).pvalue)          # assumes normality\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        levene_p_saap.append(stats.levene(*arrs, center='median').pvalue)  # robust to non-normality\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "bp, lp = np.array(bartlett_p_saap), np.array(levene_p_saap)\n",
    "print(f\"--- (A) Per-SAAP equal-variance across ages (% of tested SAAPs rejecting H0 at p<={SIG_ALPHA}) ---\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Bartlett (assumes normal) : tested={len(bp):4d}   reject={np.mean(bp<=SIG_ALPHA)*100:5.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Levene   (robust, median) : tested={len(lp):4d}   reject={np.mean(lp<=SIG_ALPHA)*100:5.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"  (rejection rate near {SIG_ALPHA*100:.0f}% ~ chance -> equal-variance pooling for the per-SAAP tests is justified)\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# (B) pooled/global: all replicate RAAS pooled per age (mirrors the 'Global RAAS by age' framing in cell 50)\n",
    "pooled = {a: v['Reporter_RAAS'].values for a, v in raas_rep_df.groupby('Sample Type', observed=True)}\n",
    "base = pooled[BASELINE_AGE]\n",
    "print(f\"--- (B) Bartlett's Test (pooled RAAS, each aged age vs {BASELINE_AGE}; assumes normal) ---\")\n",
    "for a in AGED_AGES:\n",
    "    if a not in pooled:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    stat, p = stats.bartlett(pooled[a], base)\n",
    "    print(f\"  {a} vs {BASELINE_AGE}: Statistic = {stat:.4f}, p-value = {p:.4e}  (n={len(pooled[a])} vs {len(base)})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ages_present = [a for a in AGE_ORDER if a in pooled]\n",
    "stat_lev, p_lev = stats.levene(*[pooled[a] for a in ages_present], center='median')\n",
    "print(f\"\\n--- (B) Levene's Test (pooled RAAS, all ages together; robust, center='median') ---\")\n",
    "print(f\"  {', '.join(ages_present)}: Statistic = {stat_lev:.4f}, p-value = {p_lev:.4e}\")"
   ]
  },
